#: ../../README.md:2
msgid "Docs Template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:4
msgid ""
"Sphinx documentation template for C++ projects: Markdown (MyST) pages, "
"Doxygen/Breathe/Exhale C++ reference, multi-language support via gettext,"
" and multi-version site builds from git tags. Use this repo as a template"
" (\"Use this template\" on GitHub, or clone and strip the `.git` "
"directory) to get a configured docs site for a new project in minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:10
msgid "Quick start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:17
msgid ""
"`make live` serves a live-rebuild preview at `http://localhost:8000` "
"(built into `pages-local/`); `make pages` builds the deployable multi-"
"version site into `pages/` — released-version sites (`pages/<tag>/`) only"
" exist there, so the preview's version switcher offers just `dev`. The "
"Doxygen binary is required for the C++ reference (`brew install doxygen` "
"on macOS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:24
msgid "Configure your project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:26
msgid "Work through this checklist after cloning from the template:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:28
msgid ""
"**Project identity** — set `project`, `author`, `copyright`, and "
"`release` in `docs/conf.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:30
msgid ""
"**Site URL** — set `html_baseurl` in `docs/conf.py` to your deployed site"
" (for GitHub Pages: `https://<user>.github.io/<repo>/`), and the "
"`source_repository` / `footer_icons` URLs in `docs/conf.py` to your "
"repository — they drive the header \"edit this page\" icon and the footer"
" link. Branding goes in `docs/conf.py` (`html_logo`, `html_favicon`) and "
"`docs/_static/custom.css` (accent colors)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:36
msgid "**Doxygen project name** — set `PROJECT_NAME` in `Doxyfile`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:37
msgid ""
"**C++ sources** — point `INPUT` in `Doxyfile` at your sources, then "
"replace the sample `src/example.hpp` (or delete `src/` and adjust "
"`INPUT`). The C++ reference is regenerated automatically on every build; "
"see `docs/code-reference.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:41
msgid ""
"**Languages** — edit `LANGUAGES` and `LANG_NAMES` in the `Makefile`, the "
"`docs_languages` / `docs_language_names` defaults and the `dev_banner` "
"translations in `docs/conf.py`, then run `make update` to generate `.po` "
"files under `docs/locales/` and translate them. English needs no `.po` "
"files; untranslated strings fall back to English."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:46
msgid ""
"**Pages** — write documentation as Markdown in `docs/`. The template "
"ships stubs for the common pages (getting started, architecture with a "
"mermaid diagram, changelog); fill them in and add new pages to the "
"toctree in `docs/index.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:50
msgid ""
"**Deployment** — deploy `pages/` (e.g. a GitHub Pages workflow that runs "
"`make pages` and publishes the output). Released versions come from `v*` "
"git tags; the working tree is published as the `dev` version at the site "
"root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:55
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../README.md:74
msgid ""
"Generated at build time (git-ignored): `doxygen-xml/`, `docs/api/`, "
"`docs/gettext/`, `pages/`, `pages-local/`, `.versions/`."
msgstr ""

